# The state of an actuator module's hardware interlocks, read back from their
# trip lines. The interlocks act without the MCU (ADR-0015 d11, ADR-0031 d7);
# this record reports them and nothing else.
#
# Bit n of each mask is the module's n-th interlock line; which trip that is
# belongs to the module specification. `latched` holds every line that has
# tripped since the node started, so a trip shorter than the publication
# period is still seen.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
uint8 tripped          # lines tripped now
uint8 latched          # lines tripped at any time since reset
@extent 16 * 8
